in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @mirror/store

# @mirror/au — the Fate-emitted form; the proposed-shard lifecycle
# position before settle through the property chain.
#
# Recognition (docs/specs/au-and-conductivity.md): au IS gold at the
# artifact altitude. Same operation (settle) applied at different
# altitudes produces different au:
#   au(@code/rust)   is a binary
#   au(@release)     is a signed archive
#   au(@ci/github)   is an action YAML
# The altitude parametrizes the emit; au is the type of the
# proposed-shard form. Per the spec's thesis: au IS the output type
# of @fate inference. The five Fate models do not return strings,
# ASTs, decisions, or text; they return au values — Fate-emitted
# splinters in a proposed composition. Verification is a predicate
# over au (conductivity), not a type-level transform producing a
# different kind.
#
# Relationship to `splinter` and `shard` (per docs/specs/mosaic-as-
# type-system.md §2.3, sharpened 2026-06-06 by Alex's three-layer
# recognition):
#
# au is a Fate-emitted composition of splinters. settle composes
# those splinters through the property chain and produces a shard
# (SpectralUuid-addressed; stored). The distinction is **lifecycle
# position, not type altitude**:
#
#   au       — what Fate emits. A proposed composition of splinters
#              (each splinter: content-addressed; declared altitude;
#              transparency carries whatever inference left
#              unverified). Uncommitted in the sense that the
#              property chain has not yet been run.
#   shard    — what @mirror/store keeps after settle. The SpectralUuid-
#              addressed settlement of the composed splinters.
#              Committed in the sense that settle has run the
#              splinters through the property chain and the verdict
#              landed.
#   settle   — the act of running au's splinters through the
#              compiler and the property chain. Settling IS
#              verification. As a Kleisli arrow in the Imperfect
#              monad (shards/glass.mirror's imperfect(a, e, l)):
#                settle: au → Imperfect<shard>
#              with Pass → shard committed (SpectralUuid assigned;
#              transparency = success); Partial → shard committed
#              with located transparency (opacity_map carried as the
#              residual); Failure → au stays in Fate's buffer for
#              the next kintsugi tick.
#
# The settlement transition:
#
#   au (Fate-emitted splinters, uncommitted)
#      ↓ settle (property-chain run; verify; commit)
#   Imperfect<shard> (SpectralUuid-identified, stored)
#
# Type-level discipline distinguishing au from shard lives at
# SpectralUuid validity in the target OID graph, enforced by the
# property chain at commit time. au's `content: oid` (the carrier of
# the proposed composition's address) is whatever Fate computed;
# shard's identity IS a SpectralUuid by construction (per @glass's
# shard declaration). The substrate-pull-realize lift of au's
# `content: oid` is NOT needed — au stays oid-carried because au is
# pre-commitment; shard.id is the SpectralUuid-typed slot that the
# settle transition fills. Per docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md
# §9.7's resolution at the shard layer.
#
# Reconciliation with mosaic.mirror (C2): mosaic's algebraic claim
#   type au(altitude) = settle(altitude)
# is what au IS at the build altitude — the settle operation's
# return-shape at the proposal phase, parametric over altitude.
# This shard provides the concrete record form that realizes the
# algebra against the @mirror/store. The mosaic equation is the
# substrate-pull statement; the record form below is the
# substrate-pull realization.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/au-and-conductivity.md (the type Fate
# produces; gold is the metal that conducts; au is the type that
# carries), docs/specs/mosaic.md (settle emitter -> au), the
# transparency floor in shards/glass.mirror.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-au-conductivity]] (au is the
#                      Fate output type; gold conducts; verification
#                      IS conductivity in context).
# Related shards: glass.mirror (transparency / imperfect carrier),
#                 store.mirror (oid — au's content-address carrier),
#                 mosaic.mirror (the build altitude that emits au).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/au.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/au` and only that.

prism @mirror/au {
  focus au
  project au
  split au
  shift au
  settle au
}

# === au at an altitude — the concrete record form ===
#
# au is parametric over altitude. au(@code/rust), au(@release), and
# au(@ci/github) are distinct types (the altitude is part of the
# type, not a runtime tag). The record below is what each au(A)
# resolves to: a Fate-emitted composition of splinters proposed for
# settlement at altitude A.
#
#   content       — the proposed artifact, content-addressed in the
#                   @mirror/store at the carrier level. The bytes
#                   live behind the oid; au carries the reference,
#                   not the payload. The carrier composes the
#                   splinter set Fate emitted; settle is what
#                   verifies that composition and produces a shard.
#   altitude      — which altitude this au was emitted at. `ref` is
#                   the substrate's altitude-reference carrier; the
#                   altitude is what the type-parameter `A` binds.
#   transparency  — residual opacities, if any. Per glass.mirror's
#                   transparency<p>, success means Fate's emission
#                   was clean (no proposed opacity); partial/failure
#                   carries the opacity map settle and kintsugi read
#                   to pick the next focus.
#
# Identity contract: au's identity IS the content-hash of
# (altitude, content, transparency). Per the substrate's content-
# addressing (shards/store.mirror, shards/prism.mirror's spectral-
# triple framing under CoincidenceHash<5,5>), an au value settles
# to a single oid under hashing of its three fields. Two au values
# with the same (altitude, content, transparency) are the same
# au — byte-equal at the oid. This is the substrate-level statement
# of relational entanglement: change the altitude or the residual
# transparency and you get a different au, even if `content` is the
# same bytes.
#
# After settle:
#   au's splinters → composed → SpectralUuid computed → shard
# The shard's SpectralUuid is the substrate's stored identifier;
# au's oid was the proposed-composition's content hash. Same content,
# different lifecycle phase: au's oid is the proposal address; the
# shard's SpectralUuid is the settled address.
type au(altitude) = {
  content: oid,
  altitude: ref,
  transparency: transparency(altitude),
}

# === surface ===
#
# identity(a) -> oid
#   au's content-address. The substrate computes the oid by hashing
#   (altitude, content, transparency); two au values with equal
#   identity ARE the same au. The contract above made operational.
identity(a: au) -> oid { \ }

# verify(a) -> verdict
#   The conductivity check at au's home altitude. Per au-and-
#   conductivity.md: verification IS conductivity in context;
#   `verify` reduces au's transparency over the altitude's property
#   set to a single verdict. `pass` means the residual opacity
#   weighs zero (the settle is clean; the resulting shard's
#   transparency = success); `partial(c)` means the settle is
#   conducting at confidence c (the shard's transparency carries the
#   located opacity_map); `failure(r)` means the au does not carry
#   signal at this altitude (no shard committed; au stays in Fate's
#   buffer).
verify(a: au) -> verdict { \ }

# shatter(a) -> ref
#   Project au onto the .shatter disk form (per mosaic.md §7 and
#   the forward reference to shards/mirror/shatter.mirror). The
#   substrate writes a five-section file holding the splinters'
#   composition, the transparency, the properties, the kernel, and
#   the fate of the proposed/settled composition. .shatter IS the
#   disk projection of au + splinter + mosaic (per docs/shatter-
#   spec.md's header); this action is the projection itself.
shatter(a: au) -> ref { \ }

out @mirror/au
out au
out identity
out verify
out shatter
